      "writtenOn": "2013-03-10T10:38:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first glance, one would think that this and the trust_id should be foreign keys.  I suspect the reason they are not is that since  the physical deletion of tokens from the DB is an out-of-band exercise, having a FK relationship might be problematic. On the flip side, if a provider REALLY wanted full auditing, then they would want all the entities to which the tokens are related to hang around too - however, I\u0027m not sure we want to really enforce all that (and if we did we would probably need significant additional support for the operations of archiving whole batches of related entities) \n\nProbably worth a comment here about why these attributes are not FKs",
      "revId": "481851b1516457ce2b3e03c7768277238b3864e6",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
